ere are three pairs of like terms:\n\n- $a$ and $-8a$ are like terms because they both contain the variable $a.$\n\n- $2b$ and $-10b$ are like terms because they both contain the variable $b.$\n\n- $3$ and $-9$ are like terms because they both contain no variable." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186079416 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186079522 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186079416 #edb/ref 1061 669614 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186079416 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "deb2e31e-6ff8-541f-9e7c-df91c6033fb3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186079416 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186079609 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186079418 #edb/ref 1061 669623 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186079418 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "78685eef-0c38-5b93-b9c9-d6fcdce7fb2b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186079418 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186078506 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186079419 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186079524 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186079419 #edb/ref 1061 669619 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186079419 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "28b1904c-01fc-5896-8cc6-c6e1339160bb" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186079419 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186078507 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186079522 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186079523 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186079522 #edb/ref 1061 669615 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186079522 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "cfc957cf-190f-528a-80f0-2faf92179217" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186079522 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186078572 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186079523 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186079419 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186079523 #edb/ref 1061 669618 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186079523 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "4ec7c8ab-e45c-53e4-aab7-9f47bef74302" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186079523 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186079628 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186079524 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186079418 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186079524 #edb/ref 1061 669622 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186079524 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "06c9ea06-b129-5e3c-8a12-fcef8fd2fb29" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186079524 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186079629 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186079609 #edb/ref 1064 "Terms in a linear expression are called **like terms** if their variable part is the same. For example, in the linear expression\n\n$$\n{\\color{blue}2x}+3y{\\color{blue}-5x},\n$$\n\nthe terms ${\\color{blue}2x}$ and ${\\color{blue}-5x}$ are like terms because both terms contain the same variable $x.$\n\nA linear expression may also contain multiple groups of like terms. For example, in the expression\n\n$$\n2a + \\dfrac{1}{2}b + 3a - 0.4 b - a,\n$$\n\nwe have two groups of like terms:\n\n- $2a,$ $3a,$ and $-a$ are like terms because they all contain the variable $a.$\n\n- $\\dfrac{1}{2}b$ and $-0.4b$ are like terms because they both contain the variable $b.$\n\n**Remember:** When a term has a subtraction symbol $(-)$ in front of it, the term is treated as a *negative*." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186079609 #edb/ref 1065 1352 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186079609 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "dd5dd68d-3a84-5088-8ffe-a4f52618d31e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186079609 #edb/ref 1067 "Introduction" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186079628 #edb/ref 1064 "In some expressions, there are no like terms. For example, in the expression \n\n$$\na+2b\n$$\n\n there are two terms, $a$ and $2b$. These two terms do not have the same variable part, so they are not like terms." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186079628 #edb/ref 1065 1699 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186079628 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "5bfd8a6b-a049-550a-848e-9c936685c24b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186079628 #edb/ref 1067 "Expressions with No Like Terms" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186079629 #edb/ref 1064 "*Constants are like terms, even though they do not contain variables.*\n\nTo understand why this is, remember that two terms are called like terms if they share the same variable part.\n\nAll constants have no variables, so technically they do share the same variable part. Their variable part consists of no variables at all!" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186079629 #edb/ref 1065 1700 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186079629 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "09d3ea5a-55b8-51b8-8c8b-39642db6a8e6" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186079629 #edb/ref 1067 "Constants are Like Terms" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186444842 #edb/ref 1080 "No like terms" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186444842 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186444842 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "05878f37-134d-59b9-8f6b-daa44ae9eca0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186444843 #edb/ref 1080 "$10$ and $10x$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186444843 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186444843 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "121c5493-ec8e-5d78-ae0c-e87c7710e2d1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186444844 #edb/ref 1080 "5" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186444844 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186444844 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "133b772f-765b-5463-9238-333375439ba6" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186444845 #edb/ref 1080 "$2y$ and $y$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186444845 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186444845 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "18cd95de-1fea-58f8-8ec4-e41863840306" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186444846 #edb/ref 1080 "1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186444846 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186444846 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "1a4d5dde-dec3-5bd0-bc98-11f4d40df504" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186444847 #edb/ref 1080 "4" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186444847 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186444847 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "1d6fb221-0334-5ada-8a0d-1fcb2eb0fcf8" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186444848 #edb/ref 1080 "$y$ and $49y$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186444848 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186444848 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "265ee