6920-5b6c-9601-bce23809d1f2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186444878 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186444875 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186444878 #edb/ref 1069 "q-27261" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186444878 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186444878 #edb/ref 1071 "Which of $10$, $10x$, $y$, and $49y$ are like terms?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186444878 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "89bdaeba-7457-5931-94c9-4ac589ccd204" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186444878 #edb/ref 1074 "$y$ and $49y$ are like terms since they contain the same variable ($y$)." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186444879 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186444877 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186444879 #edb/ref 1069 "q-243" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186444879 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186444879 #edb/ref 1071 "How many pairs of like terms are present in the expression $2x-4y+3-7x+10y-5$?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186444879 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "aaf35c78-310f-5644-af7b-d8eed5daf52f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186444879 #edb/ref 1074 "There are three pairs of like terms:  the $x$ terms, the $y$ terms, and the constant terms $3$ and $-5$." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186444880 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186444873 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186444880 #edb/ref 1069 "q-21823" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186444880 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186444880 #edb/ref 1071 "The like terms in the expression $-x+2y+z+5y$ are" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186444880 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "b065b0a1-2f69-56d2-893c-84bf7f3f3787" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186444880 #edb/ref 1074 "The like terms are $2y$ and $5y$ because they are both terms of the variable $y.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186444881 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186444874 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186444881 #edb/ref 1069 "q-67068" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186444881 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186444881 #edb/ref 1071 "What are the like terms in the expression $3h-v+7u+3t+5x?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186444881 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "b1195c4e-bdb0-5fa7-bea2-b175640ceb43" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186444881 #edb/ref 1074 "We write the terms of the expression as follows:\n\n$$\n(3h)+(-v)+(7u)+(3t)+(5x).\n$$\n\nNone of these terms have the same variable part. Consequently, there are no like terms in this expression." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186444882 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186444872 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186444882 #edb/ref 1069 "q-75670" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186444882 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186444882 #edb/ref 1071 "How many pairs of like terms are in the expression $6p-3+5q-2p-3q+1?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186444882 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "b4754c7a-8749-5793-bafb-b31cee518a08" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186444882 #edb/ref 1074 "We write the terms of the expression as follows:\n\n$$\n(6p)+(-3)+(5q)+(-2p)+(-3q)+(1)\n$$\n\nThere are three pairs of like terms:\n\n- $6p$ and $-2p$ are like terms because they both contain the variable $p.$\n\n- $5q$ and $-3q$ are like terms because they both contain the variable $q.$\n\n- $-3$ and $1$ are like terms because they both contain no variable." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186444883 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186444876 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186444883 #edb/ref 1069 "q-101748" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186444883 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186444883 #edb/ref 1071 "What are the like terms in the expression $8x-9y+10z+8$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186444883 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "d0f76c69-d8c0-5996-bfc8-0e524b6847e9" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186444883 #edb/ref 1074 "We write the terms of the expression as follows:\n\n$$\n(8x)+(-9y)+(10z)+(8).\n$$\n\nNone of these terms have the same variable part. Consequently, there are no like terms in this expression." #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
